  {
    "id": "doc_arch_rfc",
    "title": "RFC 042: High Performance Document Storage & Sync",
    "ownerId": "usr_sarah",
    "ownerName": "Sarah Chen",
    "ownerEmail": "sarah@ajaia.io",
    "content": "<h1>RFC 042: High Performance Document Storage &amp; Sync</h1><p><strong>Author:</strong> Sarah Chen, Principal Architect<br><strong>Status:</strong> Approved for Implementation</p><h2>1. Problem Statement</h2><p>Traditional document editors face challenges when balancing quick local responsiveness with server persistence. When multiple team members work on a document, latency and conflict resolution must be handled gracefully.</p><h2>2. Architectural Decisions</h2><ol><li><p><strong>Structured Content Storage:</strong> We preserve rich text formatted as clean HTML/JSON nodes, enabling fast roundtrips and standard web accessibility.</p></li><li><p><strong>Role-Based Access Boundaries:</strong> Permissions are strictly verified at both API endpoints and client controls. Viewers are blocked from mutation payloads.</p></li><li><p><strong>Pluggable Storage Layer:</strong> A decoupled file-backed repository pattern that seamlessly upgrades to Postgres or Neon in production.</p></li></ol><pre><code>// Pseudocode: Permission Check\nfunction canEdit(doc, user) {\n  if (doc.ownerId === user.id) return true;\n  return doc.collaborators.some(c =&gt; c.userId === user.id &amp;&amp; c.role === 'editor');\n}</code></pre>",
    "plainTextPreview": "RFC 042: High Performance Document Storage &amp; Sync Author: Sarah Chen, Principal Architect Status: Approved for Implementation 1. Problem",
    "collaborators": [
      {
        "userId": "usr_alex",
        "email": "alex@ajaia.io",
        "name": "Alex Rivera",
        "role": "editor",
        "addedAt": "2026-11-08T12:43:06.115Z"
      }
    ],
